# React Patterns (stride-desktop / stride-mobile)

## Styling

**BaseUI + CSS Modules — no Tailwind, no shadcn/ui.**

- Use [Base UI](https://base-ui.com) for unstyled/accessible primitives (dialogs, dropdowns, popovers, etc.)
- Style with CSS Modules: one `ComponentName.module.css` file per component
- Import styles as `styles` and apply via `className={styles.foo}`
- Never use inline style objects except for dynamic values (e.g. calculated widths)

```typescript
import styles from './TaskCard.module.css';

export function TaskCard({ task }: TaskCardProps) {
  return (
    <div className={styles.card}>
      <span className={styles.title}>{task.title}</span>
    </div>
  );
}
```

CSS Module files are named `PascalCase.module.css` to match their component.

## Component Conventions

**Named function exports — no default exports:**

```typescript
// CORRECT
export function TodayView() {
  return <div>...</div>;
}

// WRONG
export default function TodayView() { ... }
const TodayView = () => { ... }; export default TodayView;
```

**Props type with `Props` suffix:**

```typescript
type TaskCardProps = {
  task: Task;
  onStart?: () => void;
  className?: string;
};

export function TaskCard({ task, onStart, className }: TaskCardProps) {
  // ...
}
```

## File Organization

```
stride-desktop/src/
  pages/           # Top-level route views (TodayView, ProjectView, etc.)
  components/
    shared/        # Reusable across features
    {feature}/     # Feature-specific (auth/, navigation/, etc.)
  hooks/           # Custom hooks (useAuth.ts, useSyncStatus.ts)
  contexts/        # React contexts (AuthContext, WorkspaceContext)
  layouts/         # Layout wrappers
  lib/             # Non-React utilities, DB init (db.ts)
```

## Data Fetching — PowerSync

**All reactive DB reads use `useQuery` from `@powersync/react`:**

```typescript
import { useQuery } from '@powersync/react';

export function TaskList({ userId }: { userId: string }) {
  const { data: tasks, isLoading, error } = useQuery(
    'SELECT * FROM tasks WHERE user_id = ? AND deleted = 0 ORDER BY created_at DESC',
    [userId]
  );

  if (isLoading) return <Spinner />;
  if (error) return <ErrorMessage error={error} />;

  return <ul>{tasks.map(task => <TaskCard key={task.id} task={task} />)}</ul>;
}
```

**Rules:**
- `useQuery` for reactive reads (auto-updates when tables change)
- `useSuspenseQuery` for Suspense-compatible reads
- `useStatus` for sync connection status
- `usePowerSync` for direct DB access in hooks
- `PowerSyncContext.Provider` MUST wrap all components that use these hooks
- Do NOT build custom watch/refresh hooks — use the official `@powersync/react` hooks
- Do NOT use refresh counters, polling, or callback-based refresh patterns

## Mutations

All writes go through services from `@stridetime/core` — never call repo methods directly from UI:

```typescript
import { taskService } from '@stridetime/core';
import { usePowerSync } from '@powersync/react';

export function CreateTaskForm() {
  const db = usePowerSync();

  async function handleSubmit(data: CreateTaskInput) {
    try {
      await taskService.create(db, data);
    } catch (err) {
      handleServiceError(err);
    }
  }
}
```

## Error Handling in Components

```typescript
import { ValidationError, NotFoundError, PermissionError } from '@stridetime/types';

try {
  await taskService.create(db, params);
} catch (err) {
  if (err instanceof ValidationError) {
    setFieldError(err.field, err.message);
  } else if (err instanceof NotFoundError) {
    setError('Item not found');
  } else if (err instanceof PermissionError) {
    setError("You don't have access");
  } else {
    throw err; // Let ErrorBoundary handle unknown errors
  }
}
```

## State Management Rules

| State type | Where it lives |
|---|---|
| Server/DB data | `useQuery` from `@powersync/react` |
| Ephemeral UI state | `useState` (modal open, form inputs, loading flags) |
| Cross-component state | React Context (`src/contexts/`) |
| Timer state | `TimerContext` stores `startedAt` timestamp — display components run their own `setInterval` |

## Custom Hooks

```typescript
// src/hooks/useAuth.ts
export function useAuth() {
  const context = useContext(AuthContext);
  if (context === undefined) {
    throw new Error('useAuth must be used within an AuthProvider');
  }
  return context;
}
```

- All custom hooks live in `src/hooks/`
- Hooks that wrap a context always throw if used outside the provider
- Hooks are named `useSomething` — always camelCase with `use` prefix
